# Helm for WebCLAP

Helm by Matt Tytel, a polyphonic subtractive synthesizer, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official Helm release.

- Helm: https://github.com/mtytel/helm (commit abdedd5, version 0.9.0)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-helm.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 3 or later** (`LICENSE`), Helm's license.
It contains no JUCE: `module.wasm` is Helm's engine (mopo and its synthesis code), changed by
`patches/helm-webclap.patch`, behind the port's CLAP wrapper; the editor is the port's own web page.

The factory patches (`ui/patches.json`, converted from Helm's `patches/Factory Presets`) are licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License** (`licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt`), each by the author it names.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

